<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<swf version="8" compressed="0">
  <!--
    droptarget_scripted — gate-inventory cluster "drag: _droptarget + virtual
    position" (action.c:32895 in actionEndDrag, action.c:70182 in the
    startDrag opcode arm).

    Stage 320x240. `b` is a red 80x80 sprite covering the stage origin (0,0)
    at depth 1; `a` is a blue 40x40 sprite also at the origin at depth 2 —
    the clip that gets dragged. `mk` is a green 20x20 verdict marker.

    DoAction (frame 1) — no mouse input at all, so the drag hotspot stays at
    the default mouse position (0,0):
        startDrag("a", false, false)
        stopDrag()
        trace("PROBE:dt=" + getProperty("a", _droptarget))
        setProperty("/mk", _x, (getProperty("a",_droptarget) == "/b") / 0.005)

    The drag target is the BARE name "a", not "/a": actionEndDrag stores the
    computed path on the clip it finds by instance name, taking the tail after
    the last '.' of g_drag_target_name. A leading-slash path has no '.', so
    the lookup is done with the literal "/a", finds nothing, and _droptarget
    is never written — the probe would read "" on every build and adjudicate
    nothing. (That leading-slash miss is a separate native-side quirk, not the
    gate under test; noted in the README row.)

    NO_GRAPHICS / OFFSCREEN_RENDER: actionEndDrag calls ng_compute_droptarget
    with the virtual hotspot, finds `b` under (0,0) skipping the dragged clip
    itself, and _droptarget becomes "/b" — marker at x=200.

    browser-WASM: both the hotspot initialisation (startDrag) and the whole
    droptarget computation (stopDrag) are inside
    `#if defined(NO_GRAPHICS) || defined(OFFSCREEN_RENDER)`, so _droptarget
    stays "" and the marker sits at x=0.

    CAVEAT, read the README row before trusting a red here: Ruffle derives
    _droptarget from its mouse-driven update_drag, which never runs without
    pointer input. If the Ruffle reference disagrees with our native build,
    the divergence being measured is ours-vs-ours, not a Flash gap — the
    probe's verdict is then "couldn't probe", not "bug".
  -->
  <Header framerate="12" frames="1">
    <size>
      <Rectangle left="0" right="6400" top="0" bottom="4800"/>
    </size>
    <tags>
      <SetBackgroundColor>
        <color><Color red="220" green="220" blue="220"/></color>
      </SetBackgroundColor>

      <DefineShape objectID="1">
        <bounds><Rectangle left="0" right="1600" top="0" bottom="1600"/></bounds>
        <styles>
          <StyleList>
            <fillStyles>
              <Solid><color><Color red="220" green="40" blue="40"/></color></Solid>
            </fillStyles>
            <lineStyles/>
          </StyleList>
        </styles>
        <shapes>
          <Shape>
            <edges>
              <ShapeSetup x="0" y="0" fillStyle0="1"/>
              <LineTo x="1600" y="0"/>
              <LineTo x="0" y="1600"/>
              <LineTo x="-1600" y="0"/>
              <LineTo x="0" y="-1600"/>
              <ShapeSetup/>
            </edges>
          </Shape>
        </shapes>
      </DefineShape>

      <DefineShape objectID="2">
        <bounds><Rectangle left="0" right="800" top="0" bottom="800"/></bounds>
        <styles>
          <StyleList>
            <fillStyles>
              <Solid><color><Color red="40" green="40" blue="220"/></color></Solid>
            </fillStyles>
            <lineStyles/>
          </StyleList>
        </styles>
        <shapes>
          <Shape>
            <edges>
              <ShapeSetup x="0" y="0" fillStyle0="1"/>
              <LineTo x="800" y="0"/>
              <LineTo x="0" y="800"/>
              <LineTo x="-800" y="0"/>
              <LineTo x="0" y="-800"/>
              <ShapeSetup/>
            </edges>
          </Shape>
        </shapes>
      </DefineShape>

      <DefineShape objectID="3">
        <bounds><Rectangle left="0" right="400" top="0" bottom="400"/></bounds>
        <styles>
          <StyleList>
            <fillStyles>
              <Solid><color><Color red="20" green="180" blue="60"/></color></Solid>
            </fillStyles>
            <lineStyles/>
          </StyleList>
        </styles>
        <shapes>
          <Shape>
            <edges>
              <ShapeSetup x="0" y="0" fillStyle0="1"/>
              <LineTo x="400" y="0"/>
              <LineTo x="0" y="400"/>
              <LineTo x="-400" y="0"/>
              <LineTo x="0" y="-400"/>
              <ShapeSetup/>
            </edges>
          </Shape>
        </shapes>
      </DefineShape>

      <DefineSprite objectID="4" frames="1">
        <tags>
          <PlaceObject2 replace="0" depth="1" objectID="1"/>
          <ShowFrame/>
          <End/>
        </tags>
      </DefineSprite>

      <DefineSprite objectID="5" frames="1">
        <tags>
          <PlaceObject2 replace="0" depth="1" objectID="2"/>
          <ShowFrame/>
          <End/>
        </tags>
      </DefineSprite>

      <DefineSprite objectID="6" frames="1">
        <tags>
          <PlaceObject2 replace="0" depth="1" objectID="3"/>
          <ShowFrame/>
          <End/>
        </tags>
      </DefineSprite>

      <PlaceObject2 replace="0" depth="1" objectID="4" name="b">
        <transform><Transform transX="0" transY="0"/></transform>
      </PlaceObject2>
      <PlaceObject2 replace="0" depth="2" objectID="5" name="a">
        <transform><Transform transX="0" transY="0"/></transform>
      </PlaceObject2>
      <PlaceObject2 replace="0" depth="3" objectID="6" name="mk">
        <transform><Transform transX="0" transY="4000"/></transform>
      </PlaceObject2>

      <DoAction>
        <actions>
          <PushData>
            <items>
              <StackBoolean value="0"/>
              <StackBoolean value="0"/>
              <StackString value="a"/>
            </items>
          </PushData>
          <StartDrag/>
          <StopDrag/>

          <PushData>
            <items>
              <StackString value="PROBE:dt="/>
              <StackString value="a"/>
              <StackFloat value="14.0"/>
            </items>
          </PushData>
          <GetProperty/>
          <AddTyped/>
          <Trace/>

          <PushData>
            <items>
              <StackString value="/mk"/>
              <StackFloat value="0.0"/>
              <StackString value="a"/>
              <StackFloat value="14.0"/>
            </items>
          </PushData>
          <GetProperty/>
          <PushData><items><StackString value="/b"/></items></PushData>
          <EqualTyped/>
          <PushData><items><StackDouble value="0.005"/></items></PushData>
          <Divide/>
          <SetProperty/>
          <EndAction/>
        </actions>
      </DoAction>

      <ShowFrame/>
      <End/>
    </tags>
  </Header>
</swf>
